  "itrans": "AbrahmabhuvanAllokAH punarAvartino.arjuna . mAmupetya tu kaunteya punarjanma na vidyate .. 8-16 ..",
  "translation": "The worlds beginning with the world of Brahma return again and again, Arjuna; but having reached Me, he has no birth again. (16.)\nThe worlds from the world of Brahma are for returning, O Arjuna; but there is no birth, O Kunti's son, (for him) who has come to Me. (16.)\nV. The particle A’ (from) marks a limit. The worlds from, &c.: The worlds below that of Brahma. Those that have ascended to the worlds below that of Brahma may return to the world of birth and death. (16.)\nA. In order to demonstrate the proposition that those going to the Lord do not return to birth, the Lord will be shown to be the Author of Creation, Destruction. &c. By way of introduction to this Sri Krishna says:",
